  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes to develop and evaluate first-principles kinetic models of Ru nanoparticles for ammonia synthesis that include inherent strain and diverse surface sites, in order to test whether strain-enhanced kinetic coupling between N2 dissociation and NHx hydrogenation on communicating sites can explain high catalytic activity, relax conventional scaling limitations, and guide improved Ru catalysts.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
